  "body": "What happens: `read_back` in `crates/gpu/src/binning_gpu.rs` (lines 162-164 at `ef1572114`) polls the device with `wgpu::PollType::wait_indefinitely()`. A device that does not answer blocks the calling thread with no limit. Then the CPU fallback of the binning path does not run.\n\nExpected: the poll has a time bound. A timeout is an `Err` with the reason, and the caller runs its CPU grid.\n\nEvidence: found during the work on #2627. The new stock cut kernel (`crates/gpu/src/cut_gpu.rs`, PR for #2627) uses `PollType::Wait { submission_index: Some(at), timeout: Some(CUT_WAIT) }` and a bounded `recv_timeout` on the map callback. The binning path can use the same pattern.\n\nNow there is no caller of `bin_facets` on a user path (#2621), so the defect has no user effect yet. It must be fixed before a caller is added.\n\nDone means: `binning_gpu::read_back` waits for a bounded time, a timeout gives a named `Err`, and a test pins the named error text.\n",
